From: LockPlus Vendor <vendor@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:03:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] W12: pfTun.Close wakes a blocked reader
 (netpoller-backed fd); monotonic handle numbers

T5: the socketpair end is a non-blocking *os.File, so Close wakes a Read blocked in another goroutine instead of
leaving wgTurnOff hanging (shutdown(2) does not wake a blocked read on a socketpair end). Writes still drop when
the far end is full.
T13: storeHandle issues handles from a monotonic counter (1..MaxInt32, wrapping past live ones) instead of the lowest
free slot, so a late call with a stale handle cannot reach a newer device.
NEW-4: wgTurnOnPF owns pfFd on every path. newPFTun closes it on its own errors (unix.Close before os.NewFile, the
*os.File after), wgTurnOnPF no longer closes it again, and after newPFTun succeeds only dev.Close closes it.
lockplus_w12_test.go covers all three (run by vendor.sh).
